{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-70593-r4630311","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Crab Cakes","sourcePageId":70593,"sourceRevision":"4630311","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-04-12T21:12:56Z","sourceRevisionUser":"AdoniTzedek","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Crab%20Cakes&oldid=4630311","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:38:26.034Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Appetizer recipes","Category:Deep fried recipes","Category:Halal recipes","Category:Main course recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Pescatarian recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments","Category:Recipes using bread crumb","Category:Recipes using caper","Category:Recipes using crab","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using imitation crab","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using mayonnaise","Category:Recipes using mustard powder","Category:Recipes using vegetable oil","Category:Recipes with metric units"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"76c58671db2336f531ec28c3c1ac469aad47779d618fc09644b28945de1f015d","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary\n| category = Crab recipes\n| servings = 4\n| Difficulty = 3\n| time = Prep: 15 minutes<br/>Cooking: 10 minutes\n}}{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of the United States|American Cuisine]]\n\nThis recipe is a modified version of a [http://www.chefs.com/Recipes/RecipeDetails.aspx?id=7614 crab cake recipe] found at Chefs.com.\n__NOTOC__\n==Ingredients== \n===Crab cakes===\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Pound|lb]] (450 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) [[cookbook:crab|crab]]meat or [[cookbook:Crabstick|imitation crabmeat]] \n* 1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] Italian-style [[Cookbook:Bread Crumb|breadcrumbs]] \n* ¼ cup [[cookbook:mayonnaise|mayonnaise]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[cookbook:mustard|ground mustard]] \n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Worcestershire Sauce|Worcestershire sauce]]\n* 1 [[cookbook:egg|egg]]\n* [[cookbook:salt|Salt]] to taste\n* [[cookbook:pepper|Pepper]] to taste\n* 3 cups [[cookbook:vegetable oil|vegetable oil]] \n\n===Sauce===\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:Mayonnaise|mayonnaise]]\n* 2 tsp [[Cookbook:Worcestershire Sauce|Worcestershire sauce]]\n* 2 tsp [[Cookbook:Caper|capers]], chopped \n* 1 tsp minced [[cookbook:garlic|garlic]] \n* 1 [[cookbook:lemon|lemon]], juiced \n* ½ tsp [[cookbook:lemon zest|lemon zest]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Combine crabmeat, Italian style breadcrumbs, mayonnaise, mustard, Worcestershire sauce, egg, salt, and pepper in a medium bowl for the cakes. \n# In a separate bowl, combine remaining ingredients, except the oil, to make the sauce. \n# Shape crab cake mix into 3-[[Cookbook:Inch|inch]] (7.5 [[Cookbook:Centimetre (cm)|cm]]) patties (about 2 per serving) or smaller for appetizer-size. \n# Add oil to a [[cookbook:skillet|skillet]]. \n# [[Cookbook:Pan Frying|Pan fry]] the cakes for 3–4 minutes on each side or until golden brown.\n# Remove from skillet and drain on [[Cookbook:Paper Towel|paper towels]]. \n# Serve cakes topped with the sauce.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using crab]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mayonnaise]]\n[[Category:Recipes using caper]]\n[[Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments]]\n[[Category:Deep fried recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Appetizer recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with 